From: Alessio Ferri <alessio.ferri@mythread.it>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] b43: run the periodic calibration from the N-PHY init

b43_phy_initn() ends with a two way branch on nphy->perical. The driver
sets perical to 2 during the init, so on every device the branch that is
taken is the one that tests nphy->mphase_cal_phase_id, and that one only
initialises the PAPD tables: the TX IQ/LO, RX IQ and RSSI calibrations,
which the other branch performs, never run.

brcmsmac reaches the same point through wlc_phy_cal_perical() with
PHY_PERICAL_PHYINIT and, with no multi-phase calibration pending, runs
the whole sequence in one go: TX IQ/LO, then PAPD, then RX IQ, then the
TX power control coefficients, then RSSI. The RSSI calibration is part of
the sequence because the calibration type is not PHY_PERICAL_AUTO, and it
is the reason the vendor driver calibrates the RSSI twice per init.

An MMIO capture of wl 6.30.102.7 on a BCM6362 (N-PHY rev 8, radio 2057
rev 8) shows exactly that order, and the second RSSI calibration is a
region of the capture that the port did not reproduce at all.

Do the same, limited to phy rev 8 with radio 2057 rev 8, which is the
combination the capture covers.

Verified: records #22247-#23771 (second RSSI calibration) and #23772-#26100
Link: https://github.com/aleferri/b43-6362-wip/blob/58458f8/router-data/dsl-3580l/opinit-ch1-ch6-bw20.decoded
Link: https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/tree/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmsmac/phy/phy_n.c?id=848acc8ffe1b#n25386

Signed-off-by: Alessio Ferri <alessio.ferri@mythread.it>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_n.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_n.c
@@ -6142,6 +6142,25 @@ static void b43_nphy_papd_epsilon_offset(struct b43_wldev *dev)
 		nphy->papd_epsilon_offset[core] = offset;
 }
 
+/* The vendor driver reaches its periodic calibration from the end of the PHY
+ * init, with PHY_PERICAL_PHYINIT, and with no phase pending it runs the whole
+ * sequence in one go: TX IQ/LO, then PAPD, then RX IQ, then the TX power
+ * coefficients, then RSSI. The RSSI one is part of it because the calibration
+ * type is not PHY_PERICAL_AUTO.
+ */
+static void b43_nphy_cal_perical_phyinit(struct b43_wldev *dev,
+					 struct nphy_txgains target)
+{
+	if (!b43_nphy_cal_tx_iq_lo(dev, target, true, false)) {
+		b43_nphy_papd_cal(dev);
+		if (b43_nphy_cal_rx_iq(dev, target, 2, 0) == 0)
+			b43_nphy_save_cal(dev);
+	}
+
+	b43_nphy_tx_pwr_ctrl_coef_setup(dev);
+	b43_nphy_rssi_cal(dev);
+}
+
 static int b43_phy_initn(struct b43_wldev *dev)
 {
 	struct ssb_sprom *sprom = dev->dev->bus_sprom;
@@ -6339,12 +6358,14 @@ static int b43_phy_initn(struct b43_wldev *dev)
 						b43_nphy_save_cal(dev);
 				}
 			} else if (nphy->mphase_cal_phase_id == 0) {
-				/* brcmsmac reaches the PAPD calibration from
-				 * here too, through wlc_phy_cal_perical() with
-				 * PHY_PERICAL_PHYINIT. The rest of the periodic
-				 * calibration is still a TODO.
+				/* This is where wl runs its periodic
+				 * calibration, through wlc_phy_cal_perical()
+				 * with PHY_PERICAL_PHYINIT. Only the sequence
+				 * captured on radio 2057 rev 8 is reproduced.
 				 */
-				b43_nphy_papd_cal(dev);
+				if (phy->rev == 8 && phy->radio_rev == 8)
+					b43_nphy_cal_perical_phyinit(dev,
+								     target);
 			}
 		} else {
 			b43_nphy_restore_cal(dev);

Note per il repo, non per la mailing list:

  - Gate: `phy->rev == 8 && phy->radio_rev == 8` sulla chiamata. Per ogni altro
    device il ramo resta quello di oggi, cioe' la sola `b43_nphy_papd_cal()`,
    che ha comunque il gate dentro e non fa niente.
  - Misura: harness in `test/`, flow `init`, `--global-run 132 26100`. Le op in
    comune passano da 4434 a 5949 su 22951 (19% -> 26%), in 717 blocchi contro
    466. Per regione: seconda cal RSSI **0% -> 46%** (440 op su 960), coda
    8% -> 32%, init 31% -> 36%. Le altre tre regioni non si muovono, ed e'
    atteso: dipendono da `a2`/`a3`, che non ci sono.
  - **La finestra `rssi-cal` regredisce da 11/16 a 1/16, e non e' colpa della
    patch**: l'harness registra i piani di lettura una volta per init, il port
    adesso fa la cal RSSI due volte, i piani finiscono e la seconda calcola
    coefficienti a zero. Nel primo init (quello non tracciato) quei coefficienti
    finiscono in cache, e il secondo init prende la strada del `restore`, quindi
    la finestra vede zeri. Va sistemato l'harness prima di dire che questa patch
    e' verificata: i piani vanno ricaricati per chiamata di cal, e la finestra
    vuole `anchor_nth` per scegliere quale delle due cal guarda.
  - Cosa NON fa: la cal PAPD vera. `b43_nphy_papd_cal()` resta il segnaposto di
    `0012` (reinizializza le tabelle), al posto di `wlc_phy_a4`. Manca anche il
    `precal_txgain` (in b43 e' un TODO gia' presente), il ripristino
    dell'indice di potenza in coda alla cal, e il vcocal.
  - NON provata su hardware.
